ction modal?\nWhere is the eligibility rule evaluation happening? What SCAPI endpoint is being called?\nSearch both overrides/ and node\\_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/.\n\n7. If Claude Code modifies something it shouldn't\n-------------------------------------------------\n\n1. **Stop the session** — `Ctrl+C`.\n2. **Check what changed** — `git diff --name-only`.\n3. **Assess impact** — squad-scoped files: review carefully and continue. Tier 2: flag in the PR description. Tier 1: see step 4.\n4. **Revert Tier 1 changes immediately** — `git checkout HEAD -- path/to/the/file.ts`, or `git checkout .` to revert everything.\n5. **Notify the file owner** — even after reverting, they need to know it happened.\n6. **Refine your prompt and try again** — the most common cause is an under-scoped prompt; rewrite with explicit file paths and \"do not modify any other files.\"\n\n8. Who to contact\n-----------------\n\nSee [1.2 Team Overview](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261586947) for the current team directory and contacts. Tier 1 and Tier 2 owners are listed in the repo's `AGENTS.md` Contact Map and `.claude/rules/` files.\n\n9. Quick reference card\n-----------------------\n\n| Scenario | What to do |\n| --- | --- |\n| Starting any Claude Code session | Run `/session-start` → check branch → pull develop → write scoped prompt |\n| You're on develop or main | Create a feature branch first, no exceptions |\n| You need to change a design token | Ask the UI designer — Claude Code does not touch Tier 1 theme files |\n| You need to change `useCurrentBasket` | Ask the Integration lead — Tier 1 |\n| You need to change a component the other squad owns | Message that squad's lead first |\n| Claude modified files you didn't intend | `git diff --name-only` → revert Tier 1 files → notify owners |\n| You're unsure if a file is shared | `grep -r \"import.*filename\" overrides/` |\n| You want Claude to explain code without changing it | Always say \"without modifying any files\" in your prompt |\n| You're hitting a Tier 1 file legitimately | Get owner approval → name the file explicitly → PR it |\n| You need a new package dependency | List what you need to the integration team — do not ask Claude to add it |\n| Your commit was rejected by the commit-msg hook | Fix the format: `type(scope): description` |\n| You introduced a `.js` file in `overrides/` | Stop. Convert to `.ts`/`.tsx` |\n\nAppendix — useful git commands\n------------------------------\n\nDefaultbashgit branch --show-current\ngit diff --name-only\ngit diff\ngit checkout HEAD -- path/to/file.ts\ngit checkout develop && git pull && git checkout -b feature/TICKET-description\ngit add path/to/file1.ts path/to/file2.ts",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "c92fb136-f084-45a3-9b2a-503c8101ba82",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

